UPDATE companies SET description='Up North Plastics, Inc., a subsidiary of Poly-America, operates from Cottage Grove, Minnesota. The company manufactures silage bags, grain bags, and bunker covers designed for agricultural feed storage.

The plant runs on what the company describes as state-of-the-art manufacturing equipment, processing premium-grade polyethylene resins into multi-layer films. An extensively trained quality control team performs continuous testing during production, supplemented by additional analysis in an in-house laboratory and on test farms across the United States. Finished goods move through an international distribution network supported by a fleet of more than 300 semi-trucks.

Primary customers include grain producers, beef and dairy operations, and feed managers who rely on airtight storage to preserve high-value forages and grains. The company’s grain bags are engineered to withstand the stress of dry grain, while its bunker covers combine a 2-mil Silage Shield™ layer with a 5-mil black-and-white outer layer for spoilage reduction.

Up North Plastics emphasizes two differentiators: puncture and tear resistance that exceeds foreign competitors’ products, and a service network of distributors and dealers backed by the large truck fleet to ensure bags arrive when and where they are needed.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Silage bag manufacturing", "Grain bag manufacturing", "Bunker cover manufacturing", "Multi-layer polyethylene film production", "Continuous quality control testing", "In-house laboratory testing", "Field testing on test farms", "International distribution and logistics"], "industries": ["Agriculture", "Grain production", "Dairy farming", "Beef farming", "Feed storage"], "materials": ["Polyethylene resins"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Puncture and tear resistance exceeding foreign competitors'' products", "International distributor and dealer network", "Fleet of over 300 semi-trucks for timely delivery", "In-house laboratory and field testing on test farms", "Continuous research and development"], "facts_used": ["Subsidiary of Poly-America -> /", "Headquarters in Cottage Grove, Minnesota -> /", "Manufactures silage bags, grain bags, bunker covers -> /", "Uses premium grade polyethylene resins -> /", "State-of-the-art manufacturing equipment -> /", "Continuous quality testing by trained team -> /", "In-house laboratory testing -> /", "Field testing on test farms across U.S. -> /", "International distribution network -> /", "Fleet of 300+ semi-trucks -> /", "Serves grain producers, beef and dairy producers, feed managers -> /", "Puncture/tear resistance superior to foreign competitors -> /", "Distributor/dealer network -> /", "Languages: English, Spanish -> /", "Copyright 2019 -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "At Up North Plastics, Inc., a subsidiary of Poly-America, we manufacture the highest quality silage bags, grain bags, and bunker covers.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": ["English", "Spanish"], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='up-north-plastics-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Uranus Fudge Factory & General Store began on July 2, 2015, when founder Mayor Louie Keen opened the original location on Historic Route 66 in St. Robert, Missouri. The concept was born from a dare to create a roadside destination that captured old-school Americana — fun, family, and a good laugh — and it quickly became a travel landmark halfway between St. Louis and Springfield.

The company produces fudge fresh by hand every day, offering 18 signature flavors such as pumpkin pie nut and lemon iced tea, alongside 80-plus apparel designs, snacks, and novelty gifts. Operations have expanded to three physical locations: the St. Robert flagship (with mini golf, a sideshow museum, ice cream, and the "World''s Largest Belt Buckle"); Anderson, Indiana (opened 2022 off I-69 Exit 222, adding an 18-hole mini golf course and playground); and Richmond, Indiana (opened late 2024 at I-70 Exit 156B), a 15,000-square-foot mega-store featuring a vortex tunnel, animatronic dinosaurs, a vintage bi-plane, a shooting gallery, and a dog park. An e-commerce site ships orders over $75 free within the continental U.S.

The brand serves tourists, highway travelers, families, and gift shoppers across the Midwest and beyond, drawing visitors from around the world who want to say they''ve been to Uranus. The company cites more than 20,000 five-star customer reviews as evidence of its appeal.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Fudge manufacturing (hand-made, small-batch)", "Retail store operations", "E-commerce fulfillment", "Apparel design and retail", "Food service (ice cream, snacks)", "Tourist attraction management (mini golf, museum, entertainment)"], "industries": ["Food & beverage manufacturing", "Retail", "Tourism & hospitality", "E-commerce"], "materials": ["Sugar", "Dairy", "Flavorings", "Pecans", "Pumpkin", "Chocolate"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Fresh fudge made by hand daily in 18 signature flavors", "Three destination locations on major highways (Route 66, I-69, I-70)", "Free standard shipping on online orders over $75", "Integrated entertainment: mini golf, sideshow museum, vortex tunnel, animatronics", "Broad product mix: fudge, apparel (80+ designs), snacks, novelty gifts"], "facts_used": ["Founded July 2, 2015 by Mayor Louie Keen -> /about-us", "Headquarters in St. Robert, MO (14400 State Hwy Z) -> /about-us", "Three locations: St. Robert MO, Anderson IN (2022), Richmond IN (late 2024) -> /about-us", "Richmond location is 15,000 sq ft mega-store -> /about-us", "Makes fudge fresh by hand daily, 18 signature flavors -> /about-us", "80+ apparel options -> /about-us", "20,000+ 5-star customer reviews -> /about-us", "Free standard shipping on orders over $75 in continental US -> /", "Products: fudge, snacks, apparel, gifts -> /", "Attractions: mini golf, sideshow museum, ice cream, vortex tunnel, animatronics, dog park -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Retailer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "It all started with a dream \u2014 and a dare. Our founder, Mayor Louie Keen, wanted to create a roadside destination that captured the spirit of old-school Americana: fun, family, and a good laugh. What began as a quirky pit stop for travelers has grown into a full-blown attraction with delicious fudge made fresh by hand every day.", "founded_year": "2015", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["Facebook", "YouTube", "Twitter", "Instagram"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='uranus-fudge-factory-general-store-uranus-missouri' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Utah Solar Detach & Reset operates from Kearns, Utah, serving homeowners and contractors across the Wasatch Front. The locally owned company grew out of a roofing business, giving its founders firsthand experience with the intersection of roof work and solar arrays.

The company specializes in solar panel removal and reinstallation — often called detach and reset — for roof replacements, system maintenance, or upgrades. Technicians document panel positions and wiring before any removal, then follow structured diagnostic sequences to isolate faults before replacing components. Additional services include solar panel cleaning with output verification, critter guard installation, EV charger installation, battery troubleshooting, and solar monitoring setup. Work is performed from a brick‑and‑mortar office in Kearns, with crews traveling to Sandy, Salt Lake City, West Jordan, Taylorsville, Murray, Draper, and surrounding communities.

Primary customers fall into two groups: homeowners who discover their solar arrays must be temporarily removed for roof repairs, and roofing contractors who need a reliable solar detach partner to keep their projects on schedule. Both receive transparent pricing, coordination with project timelines, and a documented process that protects roof penetrations and electrical connections.

The business was built to fill the gap between roofers who lack solar expertise and solar installers who don’t focus on detach‑and‑reset work. Its methodical, climate‑aware approach — accounting for heavy snow loads, freeze‑thaw cycles, and high‑altitude UV exposure — and its local, physical presence are cited as key differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar panel detach and reset (removal and reinstallation)", "Solar system troubleshooting and diagnostics", "Solar panel cleaning and preventative maintenance", "Critter guard installation", "EV charger installation", "Battery troubleshooting", "Solar monitoring and WiFi setup", "Roof-safe panel removal with full documentation", "Diagnostic sequences to isolate faults before replacement", "Output comparison after cleaning to verify performance"], "industries": ["Residential solar", "Roofing contractors", "Solar energy services"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Methodical documented detach and reset process", "Service tailored to Utah snow loads, freeze\u2011thaw cycles, and high\u2011altitude UV", "Roofing background informs both solar and roof integrity", "Locally owned with physical office in Kearns, UT", "Panel position and wiring documented before removal"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Kearns, UT -> /about", "Service area: Sandy, Salt Lake City, West Jordan, Taylorsville, Murray, Draper -> /about", "Locally owned and operated -> /about", "Business emerged from roofing background -> /about", "Services: detach and reset, diagnostics, cleaning, critter guard, EV charger, battery, monitoring -> / and /about", "Methodical documented process with panel position/wiring documentation -> /about", "Climate-specific design for snow loads, freeze-thaw, UV -> /about", "Primary customers: homeowners and roofing contractors -> /about", "Physical office at 5172 W Liberator Dr Ste 301, Kearns, UT 84118 -> /about", "No founding year, employee count, certifications, equipment, materials, volume, lead time, tolerances stated -> db"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Utah Solar Detach & Reset is a locally owned solar panel removal and reinstallation company serving Sandy, Salt Lake City, West Jordan, Taylorsville, Murray, and Draper.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='utah-solar-detach-reset' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='V&I Custom Furniture operates from a workshop in Menlo Park, California, serving clients throughout the Bay Area. The studio focuses on fully custom cabinetry and furniture for both residential and commercial projects.

The company designs and handcrafts a range of built-in pieces, including kitchens, closets, bathroom vanities, entertainment centers, home offices, wine storage, and shelving. All work is produced in their Menlo Park workshop using traditional joinery and finishing techniques, with each project planned around the client''s specific space and requirements. The firm also handles delivery and professional installation across the region.

V&I works directly with homeowners, interior designers, and builders, treating each project as a collaboration that emphasizes clear communication from initial consultation through final installation. The studio offers free consultations for custom cabinetry and furniture projects.

The company distinguishes itself by avoiding prefabricated or flat-pack components, instead using premium materials selected for durability and daily use. Its process centers on custom planning, handcrafted construction, and a reliable workflow that aims for a precise, seamless fit in every installation.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom cabinetry design and fabrication", "Custom furniture design and fabrication", "Handcrafted joinery", "Finishing", "Project planning and design consultation", "Delivery and installation", "Free initial consultation"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Handcrafted in Menlo Park workshop", "No prefab or flat-pack components", "Custom planning tailored to each space and lifestyle", "Professional delivery and installation across the Bay Area", "Free consultations for custom projects"], "facts_used": ["Located in Menlo Park, California -> db", "Specializes in fully custom cabinetry and furniture for residential and commercial spaces -> /", "Handcrafted in Menlo Park workshop -> /", "Uses premium materials, never prefab or flat-pack -> /", "Offers professional delivery and installation across Bay Area -> /", "Works with homeowners, designers, and builders -> /", "Offers free consultations -> /", "Creates kitchens, bedrooms, bathrooms, entertainment rooms, closets, home offices, wine storage, shelving -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "V&I Custom Furniture is a Menlo Park\u2013based studio specializing in fully custom cabinetry and furniture for residential and commercial spaces across the Bay Area.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='v-i-custom-furniture' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='VFN Fiberglass Inc. operates from Addison, Illinois, where it has been a leader in the fiberglass automotive components industry for over 50 years.

The company manufactures a wide range of fiberglass body parts for both street and drag-racing applications. Its product line includes complete door-slammer bodies, front-end assemblies, hoods, doors, trunks, bumpers, scoops, and cowl-induction hoods. Many hoods are offered as bolt-on units designed to work with factory hinges and latches, and all street hoods are bonded with aerospace-grade adhesives.

VFN serves the automotive aftermarket, focusing on drag racers and street-performance enthusiasts. Its components are built to withstand the stresses of competition while retaining factory-style detail.

The business was founded on a mission to produce lightweight, durable parts that handle the abuse of drag racing without sacrificing OEM-level fit and finish. Management emphasizes that its reputation has grown through word of mouth rather than advertising, and it points to the use of aerospace adhesives as a key differentiator for product longevity.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Fiberglass molding", "Door-slammer body fabrication", "Front-end assembly production", "Hood manufacturing (including cowl induction)", "Door, trunk, bumper, and scoop molding", "Bolt-on application engineering", "Aerospace adhesive bonding", "Custom fiberglass component design"], "industries": ["Automotive aftermarket", "Drag racing", "Street performance"], "materials": ["Fiberglass", "Aerospace-grade adhesives"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Aerospace-grade adhesives used in all street hoods", "Bolt-on hoods designed for factory hinges and latches", "Over 50 years of industry experience", "Reputation built on word of mouth with minimal advertising", "Manufactures complete door-slammer bodies and front-end assemblies"], "facts_used": ["Company name VFN Fiberglass Inc -> db", "Headquarters Addison, Illinois -> db", "Manufactures fiberglass components for street and race cars -> /", "Over 50 years in industry -> /", "Uses aerospace-grade adhesives -> /", "Bolt-on hoods using factory hinges/latches -> /", "Word-of-mouth reputation, rarely advertises -> /", "Social media presence: Facebook, YouTube, Instagram -> /", "Produces complete door slammer bodies, front ends, hoods, doors, trunks, bumpers, scoops -> /", "Serves automotive aftermarket, drag racing, street performance -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We Manufacture complete door slammer bodies, Hundreds of Complete Front ends. Thousands of Hoods, Doors, Trunks, Bumpers Scoops.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='vfn-fiberglass-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Valencia Plastics operates from Valencia, California, where it has provided custom plastic injection and blow molding services for over 20 years. The company runs a full-service facility that includes an in-house mold shop, engineering support, and assembly capabilities.

The shop produces injection-molded parts ranging from 1 gram to 7 lb shot weight and blow-molded parts from 5 grams to 5 lb. It handles multi-component molding such as over molding and insert molding, in-mold labeling, and offers short runs through full-scale production. Standard production lead time is two weeks, with same-day shipping available for stocked items.

Customers span nutritional, nutraceutical, food, pet food, aerospace, agricultural, architectural, construction, consumer goods, dental, electrical, health supplements, marine, automotive, medical, military, oil field, optical, packaging, pharmaceutical, and transportation sectors. The company also works with inventors and new product designers from concept to shelf.

