UPDATE companies SET description='Vermont Green Printing, operating as VG Printing, is a contract screen-printing and embroidery shop based in Morrisville, Vermont. The business was launched in 2014 by co-owner John Goodhue, who had spent more than three decades producing tie-dyed and screen-printed apparel for concert tours such as the Grateful Dead, Phish, and the HORDE festival, as well as wholesale accounts in the U.S. and Japan. Goodhue’s first commercial sales date back to 1983 at a Tucson street fair, and his move to Vermont marked a shift from touring merchandise to a local, service-oriented operation.

The company provides custom screen printing using water-based and algae-based inks, embroidery on caps, jackets, and fleece, full-color garment printing with a 24-piece minimum, and promotional product sourcing. Its printing process avoids plastisol and solvents, relying instead on discharge and opaque water-based inks that are free of PVC, phthalates, and heavy metals. In 2022 the shop adopted Algae Black ink, a bio-based pigment. The facility on Old Creamery Road handles both small and large runs, though specific headcount and floor space are not disclosed.

VG Printing serves a mix of regional and national clients. References on its site include Vermont Festivals LLC, the gaming brand Gamers Nexus, Riverbend Market, Green Mountain Community Fitness, the rowing-machine manufacturer Concept2, Paul’s Hardware, and the tech retailer Level One Techs. Orders range from event merchandise and corporate apparel to e-commerce fulfillment for online stores.

The company states that its founding purpose was to minimize environmental impact, pay living wages, and create products customers can feel good about. It donates at least 1% of gross sales each month to organizations such as the Vermont Food Bank, Planned Parenthood of Northern New England, The Ocean Cleanup, the Last Prisoner Project, and the Equal Justice Initiative. Goodhue’s own history — including a year in prison for cannabis cultivation — informs the shop’s support for criminal-justice reform.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Screen printing with water-based inks", "Embroidery on caps, beanies, jackets, sweatshirts", "Promotional product sourcing", "Full-color garment printing (minimum 24 pieces)", "Algae Black ink printing", "Discharge ink printing", "Opaque solvent-free ink printing"], "industries": ["Festival and event production", "Gaming and esports", "Specialty retail", "Fitness and wellness", "Manufacturing (rowing equipment)", "Hardware retail", "Technology and e-commerce"], "materials": ["Water-based inks", "Algae Black ink", "Solvent-free opaque inks", "Discharge inks", "Organic cotton apparel", "Recycled polyester apparel"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Uses water-based, solvent-free inks (including Algae Black bio-based pigment)", "Donates 1% of gross sales monthly to charitable causes", "Commits to living wages and a safe, enjoyable workplace", "Eliminates solvents in cleanup through water-based ink processes"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2014 by John Goodhue -> /about-us", "Located in Morrisville, Vermont -> /, /about-us", "Uses water-based and algae-based inks -> /, /about-us", "Offers screen printing, embroidery, promotional products, full-color printing -> /", "Customers include Vermont Festivals LLC, Gamers Nexus, Riverbend Market, Green Mountain Community Fitness, Concept2, Paul''s Hardware, Level One Techs -> /", "Mission: minimize environmental impact, pay living wages, create feel-good products -> /, /about-us", "Donates 1% of gross sales to charities monthly -> /about-us", "Adopted Algae Black ink in 2022 -> /about-us", "John Goodhue started printing in 1978, commercial sales 1983 -> /about-us", "Minimum 24 pieces for full-color printing -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Custom Screen Printing, Embroidery & Promotional Products", "founded_year": "2014", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "24 pieces (full-color printing)", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='vermont-green-printing' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
