UPDATE companies SET description='WB Manufacturing, headquartered in Thorp, Wisconsin, operates as a manufacturer of furniture and architectural casework for educational and commercial settings. The company, formerly known as Wisconsin Bench, provides design, fabrication, and delivery services from its Thorp facility.

The product line includes standard cabinets and lockers, modular casework, mobile furniture, and custom solutions tailored to specific spaces. An in-house design team works with CET design software to render rooms and integrate product specifications. The company also offers a Build & Hold program for project staging, project registration, and continuing education credit (CEU) opportunities for design professionals.

Recent projects include Paso Verde STEAM School in Sacramento, California, and Tomahawk Elementary in the Shawnee Mission School District. The company also markets its capabilities to broader commercial markets, emphasizing flexibility for any environment.

The company positions its in‑house design team and ability to handle both fixed and mobile installations as key differentiators. Its Build & Hold program allows customers to stage deliveries to match construction schedules, and the design team can import room dimensions directly into CET to furnish spaces virtually. WB Manufacturing emphasizes a "Design. Build. Deliver." approach, aiming to provide end‑to‑end service from concept through installation.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Design (in-house, CET integration)", "Manufacturing of standard cabinets and lockers", "Modular casework", "Mobile furniture", "Custom furniture solutions", "Build & Hold program", "Project registration", "CEU credit offerings"], "industries": ["Education", "K-12 schools", "Higher education", "STEAM education", "Media centers", "Art rooms"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["In-house design team with CET software integration", "Build & Hold program for staged project delivery", "Custom modular and mobile furniture solutions", "Standard cabinets, lockers, and casework lines"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Thorp, WI -> db", "Address: 507 E Grant Street, Thorp, WI 54771 -> /about", "Products: standard cabinets, lockers, modular casework, mobile furniture, custom solutions -> /", "Services: in-house design team, CET integration, Build & Hold program, project registration, CEU credit -> /services", "Industries: education, K-12 schools, STEAM labs, media centers, art rooms -> /", "Project examples: Paso Verde STEAM School (Sacramento, CA), Tomahawk Elementary (Shawnee Mission School District) -> /", "Differentiators: in-house design team, Build & Hold program, custom modular and mobile units -> /, /services", "Company type: manufacturer of furniture and casework -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "WB Manufacturing can design, build and deliver standard cabinets and lockers, modular casework, mobile furniture and custom solutions for any environment", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='wb-manufacturing-formerly-wisconsin-bench' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='WCP Solutions traces its roots to March 1, 1930, when the company began operating out of a Ford Model A in Seattle’s Pike Place Market and International District. Now a third-generation, privately owned wholesale distributor, the business serves the Pacific Northwest and beyond from multiple divisions, including the Idaho Falls location managed by division manager Brad Bolander. The Idaho Falls division covers eastern Idaho, northern Utah, and western Wyoming from its warehouse

The company distributes paper and envelopes, packaging and shipping supplies, facility and janitorial products, food-service disposables, and personal protective equipment. It also sells, integrates, and services janitorial and packaging equipment. An in-house converting and manufacturing team produces Perfect Fit® custom sheets, prototypes, and envelopes, while local warehouses and a fleet of yellow delivery trucks support next-day service across the region.

Customers range from commercial printers and creative agencies to restaurants, food processors, healthcare facilities, universities, and grocery retailers. Long-term accounts include Idahoan Foods in Idaho Falls, Kent’s Meats & Groceries in Redding, A.T. Publishing & Printing in Anchorage, the University of Oregon in Eugene, Capitol City Press in Tumwater, and Rogue Valley Medical Center in Medford.

WCP emphasizes locally based support that spans consulting, sourcing, stocking, and delivery, backed by online ordering tools. The company’s WCP Cares program directs each division to partner with a local nonprofit; the Idaho Falls division supports the 1614 Revival Foundation, a refuge for survivors of domestic violence. Sustainability initiatives include recycling all paper waste by grade, reusing wood pallets and plastic packaging, and operating a fleet that meets CARB standards with electric material-handling equipment in warehouses.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Wholesale distribution of paper, envelopes, packaging, facility supplies, food service, PPE", "Equipment sales, integration, training, parts, and service for janitorial and packaging equipment", "Custom converting and manufacturing (Perfect Fit\u00ae sheets, prototypes, envelopes)", "Online ordering and inventory management", "Warehousing and local delivery", "Sustainability consulting and sustainable product sourcing"], "industries": ["Commercial printing", "Creative agencies", "Restaurants and food service", "Food processing", "Healthcare facilities", "Higher education", "Grocery retail", "Publishing", "General business offices", "Local government and organizations"], "materials": ["Paper", "Corrugated", "Plastic films", "Wood pallets"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Locally based support from consulting through delivery", "In-house converting and manufacturing of Perfect Fit\u00ae custom sheets, prototypes, and envelopes", "Online ordering platform and fleet of yellow delivery trucks for next-day service", "Third-generation private ownership with over 95 years in business", "Community-focused WCP Cares program and sustainability initiatives (paper recycling, CARB-compliant fleet)"], "facts_used": ["Founded March 1, 1930 in Seattle''s Pike Place Market -> /about", "Third-generation privately owned company -> /about", "Idaho Falls division managed by Brad Bolander -> /", "Service area: Ashton, ID to Logan, UT to Jackson, WY -> /", "Product categories: paper, packaging, facility supplies, food service, PPE, equipment -> /", "In-house converting and manufacturing of Perfect Fit\u00ae custom sheets, prototypes, envelopes -> /about", "Local warehouses and yellow delivery trucks -> /about", "Online ordering tools -> /about", "Testimonials from Idahoan Foods, Kent''s Meats, A.T. Publishing, University of Oregon, Capitol City Press, Rogue Valley Medical Center -> /", "WCP Cares program supports 1614 Revival Foundation -> /", "Sustainability: paper waste recycling, plastic and pallet reuse, CARB-compliant fleet, electric material handling -> /about", "Leadership team: Amy Swanson (CEO), Ed Allen (President), Teresa Russell (Owner and Chairperson) -> /about"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "As a locally focused wholesale distributor, we provide products and services that help customers effectively and efficiently run their businesses.", "founded_year": "1930", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='wcp-solutions' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='WIREONE Electric operates from Pleasant Hill, Iowa, serving Greater Des Moines and Central Iowa through seven regional offices. The company’s founding year and ownership structure are not publicly disclosed.

The firm provides residential and commercial electrical services including wiring, lighting installation, electrical panel and breaker work, surge protection, outlet and switch installation, smart home technology integration, safety inspections, rewiring, ceiling fan installation, and EV charging station installation. Technicians operate from a mobile warehouse stocked with thousands of parts, enabling most jobs to be completed in a single visit. The team completes over 200 hours of continuing education annually, well above the 18-hour requirement.

The company’s blog addresses commercial electrical safety inspections, home buyer and seller inspections, and Midwest weather preparedness.

