UPDATE companies SET description='Warbler Woodworks operates from a shop in Waynesboro, Virginia, where a single craftsman designs and builds custom furniture using traditional joinery.

The shop produces heirloom-quality furniture such as wine cabinets, office desks, settees, dining tables, side tables, and credenzas. Each piece is made one at a time using time-honored techniques including dovetail and mortise-and-tenon joinery, executed with a blend of hand tools and power tools. The maker selects local hardwoods — primarily black walnut and cherry, along with white oak, maple, hickory, and ash — for their grain, color, and strength.

Warbler Woodworks serves residential clients who commission custom pieces for their homes. The shop’s reach extends across the Shenandoah Valley and into the Mid-Atlantic region, with customers in Virginia’s major cities and the Washington, D.C. metro area.

The founder emphasizes that mass-produced furniture lacks the subtlety and durability of handcrafted work. By relying on traditional joinery rather than screws or bolts, and by finishing each piece to highlight the wood’s natural character, the shop aims to create furniture that tells a story and endures for generations.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Dovetail joinery", "Mortise-and-tenon joinery", "Custom furniture design and fabrication", "Hand tool woodworking", "Power tool woodworking", "Wood selection and sourcing"], "industries": [], "materials": ["Black Walnut", "Cherry", "White Oak", "Maple", "Hickory", "Ash"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Traditional dovetail and mortise-and-tenon joinery", "Locally sourced hardwoods selected for grain and color", "One-at-a-time craftsmanship by a single maker", "Blend of hand tools and power tools", "Heirloom-quality custom furniture"], "facts_used": ["Location: Waynesboro, Virginia -> /about", "Single craftsman operation -> /about", "Traditional joinery: dovetail and mortise-and-tenon -> /about", "Materials: Black Walnut, Cherry, White Oak, Maple, Hickory, Ash -> /about", "Products: wine cabinets, desks, settees, dining tables, side tables, credenzas -> /", "Service area: Charlottesville, Harrisonburg, Richmond, Washington D.C. -> /about", "Blend of hand tools and power tools -> /about", "Focus on heirloom quality and natural wood character -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Handcrafted custom furniture made with traditional joinery.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='warbler-woodworks' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Warfield Electric was founded in 1974 in Upland, California. The company began as a specialist in DC motor repair and has since expanded into custom motor manufacturing and large-scale remanufacturing.

Today Warfield Electric operates as both a manufacturer and remanufacturer of AC and DC electric motors. Under the WEMOCO (Warfield Electric Motor Company) banner it builds custom DC motors for original equipment manufacturers, while its DC Connection division rejuvenates obsolete industrial motors and gearboxes. The company maintains six locations across the United States — Frankfort, Illinois; Upland, California; Conyers, Georgia; Waukesha, Wisconsin; Westland, Michigan; and Dallas, Texas — and stocks an inventory of over 10,000 motors available on an exchange basis. It produces new OEM DC motors for more than 15 global manufacturers and rebuilds drive units for brands such as Hyster, Yale, Crown, Toyota, and Raymond.

The company serves the wind energy sector with new pitch motors and remanufactured pitch and yaw motors for turbines from GE, AMD, SSB, Moog, Clipper, Adda, VEM, ABB, Lonne, AVN, and Bonfiglioli. In material handling it supplies remanufactured motors and drive units for forklifts and warehouse equipment. Additional markets include ground support equipment, agriculture, mining, airport facilities, cold storage, and brewery applications. Customers range from OEMs to independent repair shops such as Mahaffeys Electric Motor Repair and large fleet operators like Anderson Material Handling.

Warfield Electric emphasizes service, quality, and price as its founding principles. It promotes its remanufactured motors as engineered to or above OEM standards, highlights a knowledgeable on-site engineering staff, and stresses honest pricing to build long-term partnerships. The firm positions itself as the nation’s largest DC motor remanufacturer, leveraging a nationwide exchange program and the ability to produce custom motors in small quantities.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom DC motor manufacturing", "AC/DC motor remanufacturing", "Armature repair", "Brush replacement", "Bearing replacement", "Motor exchange programs", "Slip ring manufacturing", "Wind turbine pitch motor manufacturing", "Wind turbine yaw motor remanufacturing", "Drive unit rebuilding", "Gearbox repair", "Obsolete motor rejuvenation", "New motor parts fabrication", "Custom DC motor small quantity production"], "industries": ["Wind Energy", "Material Handling", "Industrial", "Ground Support Equipment", "Agriculture", "Mining", "Airport Facility", "Cold Storage", "Brewery Applications"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Largest DC motor remanufacturer in the nation with over 10,000 motors in stock across six U.S. locations", "Custom DC motors manufactured in small quantities for OEMs", "New OEM DC motors supplied to 15+ global manufacturers", "Remanufactured motors engineered to or above OEM standards", "Nationwide exchange program for motors and drive units"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1974 -> db", "Headquarters Upland, California -> db", "Description: Custom DC motor manufacturer serving OEM customers -> db", "Six U.S. locations (Frankfort IL, Upland CA, Conyers GA, Waukesha WI, Westland MI, Dallas TX) -> /", "Over 10,000 motors in stock across six locations -> /", "Manufactures new OEM DC motors for 15+ global manufacturers -> /", "WEMOCO custom DC motor manufacturing for OEMs -> /", "DC Connection division for obsolete industrial motors and gearboxes -> /", "Remanufactured motors engineered to or above OEM standards -> /", "Wind turbine pitch motors (new) and yaw motors (remanufactured) for brands GE, AMD, SSB, Moog, Clipper, Adda, VEM, ABB, Lonne, AVN, Bonfiglioli -> /", "Material handling motors and drive units for Hyster, Yale, Crown, Toyota, Raymond -> /", "Industries served: wind energy, material handling, industrial, ground support equipment, agriculture, mining, airport facility, cold storage, brewery applications -> /", "Armature repair, brush replacement, bearing replacement, motor exchange services -> /", "Slip ring manufacturing -> /", "Custom DC motors in small quantities -> /", "Nationwide exchange program -> /", "Testimonials from Mahaffeys Electric Motor Repair and Anderson Material Handling -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Warfield Electric boasts a dual identity as both an Electric Motor Manufacturer and Remanufacturer", "founded_year": "1974", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='warfield-electric' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Wasatch Cable & Design, LLC operates from Springville, Utah, with a design and support presence in nearby Orem. The company was founded on the principle that communication is the fabric of its business, though a specific founding year is not publicly disclosed. Ownership details beyond the LLC structure are not stated, and founder names are not provided in available materials.

The company provides end-to-end cable assembly services, from design optimization for manufacturability through production and testing. It runs domestic design, engineering, and support functions while leveraging Pacific-Rim manufacturing facilities for cost-effective turn-key production. Capabilities include custom molded assemblies with unique connectors and over-molded strain reliefs, mechanically assembled cables, wire harnesses, and smart cables incorporating PCBs or discrete components. Every assembly undergoes 100% testing and is warranted against defects, and the firm offers stocking and warehousing programs to secure on-time delivery.

