UPDATE companies SET description='Weidmann Electrical Technology is headquartered in St Johnsbury, Vermont. The company traces its origins to 1877, when it began as a manufacturer of electrical insulation. Today it operates as a global group with a 145-year history of innovation in transformer insulation.

The company produces specialized insulation technology and accessories for power transformers, including its signature Transformerboard, invented in 1937 and regarded as an industry standard. With 18 strategic facilities across 10 countries and a workforce of over 3,000, Weidmann ships more than 5 million products annually and generates annual revenue exceeding CHF 500 million. Its engineering teams collaborate with customers worldwide to develop custom insulation solutions for demanding applications.

Weidmann serves the energy sector, transformer manufacturers, and the railway industry, providing custom-designed solutions for traction transformers that emphasize efficiency and sustainability. The company also operates in electrical, medical, and fiber-optic markets, supporting critical infrastructure in more than 80 countries.

Weidmann differentiates itself through its long-standing expertise in transformer insulation, a global footprint that enables local support, and a sustainability strategy aligned with the UN Sustainable Development Goals and recognized by Ecovadis ratings. The firm emphasizes innovation with purpose, quality, and compliance as core to its partnerships.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Transformer insulation manufacturing", "Insulation component production", "Custom insulation design for railway and transformer applications", "Technical engineering collaboration", "Specialized insulation technology development", "Insulation accessories supply"], "industries": ["Energy", "Transformer", "Railway", "Electrical", "Medical", "Fiber"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "5+ million products shipped annually", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["World leader in electrical transformer insulation", "Transformerboard invented in 1937, considered the industry standard", "Global footprint: 18 facilities in 10 countries", "5+ million products shipped annually", "Sustainability strategy aligned with UN SDGs and Ecovadis ratings"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1877 -> /about", "Headquarters in St Johnsbury, Vermont -> db", "3,000+ employees worldwide -> /about", "18 strategic facilities in 10 countries -> /about", "CHF 500+ million annual revenue -> /about", "5+ million products shipped annually -> /about", "Transformerboard invented in 1937 -> /", "Serves energy sector, transformer industry, railway industry -> /, /about", "Industries: Electrical, Medical, Fiber -> /about", "Sustainability commitment to UN SDGs and Ecovadis -> /about", "World leader in electrical transformer insulation -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Weidmann Electrical Technology supplies the energy sector with best-in-class specialized insulation technology and accessories.", "founded_year": "1877", "employee_count": "3,000+", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='weidmann-electrical-technology' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Weiss Sheet Metal operates from Avon, Massachusetts, where it was founded in 1934. The family-owned business has served the New England region for nearly nine decades, building a reputation for custom sheet metal fabrication.

The company specializes in stainless steel, aluminum, brass, and copper fabrication for residential, commercial, and architectural projects. Its 27,000-square-foot facility houses in-house shearing and bending capacity for 12-foot sheets, along with laser cutting, water jet cutting, punching, forming, welding, and polishing. The shop handles orders ranging from single pieces to 1,000-unit runs and provides design support via SolidWorks and AutoCAD.

Projects have encompassed exhaust hoods, work tables, custom cabinetry, column covers, sunscreens, and bollards for clients throughout Massachusetts and surrounding states.

Weiss Sheet Metal emphasizes its family-owned, hands-on approach and a team with over 200 years of combined experience. The company cites its ability to deliver invisible welds through butt welding and polishing, on-request shop drawings, and direct job-site delivery as key differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["SolidWorks design", "AutoCAD design", "Shearing", "Laser cutting", "Water jet cutting", "Punching", "Forming", "Welding", "Polishing", "Job site delivery"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial", "Architectural", "Food service", "Laboratories", "Stadiums", "Kitchens"], "materials": ["Stainless steel", "Aluminum", "Brass", "Copper", "Steel"], "equipment": ["Shear and brake (12 ft capacity)", "Laser cutting system", "Water jet cutting system"], "volume": "1 to 1,000 units", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned, hands-on project management", "200+ years of combined team experience", "27,000 sq ft facility with 12-ft shear and brake capacity", "Laser and water jet cutting in-house", "Butt welding and polishing for invisible welds"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1934 -> /about-us", "Family-owned -> /", "27,000 sq ft facility -> /", "200+ years combined experience -> /", "Shear and bend 12'' sheets -> /about-us", "Laser and water jet cutting -> /about-us", "Butt welding and polishing invisible welds -> /about-us", "SolidWorks and AutoCAD design -> /services", "Shearing, laser cutting, water jet cutting, punching, forming, welding, polishing -> /services", "Materials: stainless steel, aluminum, brass, copper -> /", "Industries: residential, commercial, architectural, food service, laboratories, stadiums -> /", "Volume: 1 to 1,000 items -> /about-us", "Job site deliveries -> /services"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We provide stainless steel custom fabrication services to individuals and businesses in and around Avon, MA, New England and surrounding states.", "founded_year": "1934", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='weiss-sheet-metal' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Wells Wood Turning & Finishing operates from a mill in Buckfield, Maine. The company has produced souvenir mini baseball bats for 25 years, though its founding year is not publicly stated.

The shop turns custom wood components on traditional back knife lathes and finishes them on rotary sanders. Core products include mini bats (1.25-inch barrel, 18 inches long) made from yellow birch, plus rolling pins, tool handles, furniture components, craft parts, drinkware, and promotional items such as Easter eggs. Finishing options cover water-based varnish and paint; personalization uses single-color pad printing or laser engraving. The facility handles high-volume runs and national campaigns.

Customers span Major and Minor League baseball suppliers, Little League organizations, promotional-products distributors, brokers, and civic groups. All raw lumber is sourced from North American sawmills.

