UPDATE companies SET description='The company was founded by Ron Turnier, who serves as CEO, though a founding year is not publicly disclosed. The business began as a chef-centered wholesale distributor focused on eliminating traditional friction points in foodservice procurement.

The company operates as a broadline food distributor across 12 states — Alabama, Colorado, Florida, Georgia, Illinois, Indiana, Kentucky, Missouri, North Carolina, South Carolina, Ohio, and Tennessee — running 19 distribution centers that serve over 16,000 restaurants. Its seven core product lines span produce, seafood, meat, gourmet, staples, to-go, and dairy. In 2026, What Chefs Want acquired Florida-based Quality Cut Produce, adding a state-of-the-art fresh-cut processing facility and expanding its PrepKitchen operation to provide pre-portioned, ready-to-use fruits and vegetables. The distributor offers daily delivery on a six-day schedule, split-case ordering, no minimum order requirements, and 24/7 customer support via phone, text, chat, and email, all backed by a proprietary web ordering platform and mobile app.

The company’s Local Food Connection and Boat Direct programs highlight a focus on regional sourcing and direct-from-harvest seafood.

What Chefs Want positions its model on operational flexibility: removing minimums, enabling split cases, and guaranteeing rapid replenishment so chefs can order precisely what they need, reduce waste, and maintain menu creativity without inventory burden. The Quality Cut acquisition was framed as a natural extension of that vision, adding production capacity to further cut prep labor and improve consistency for foodservice operators.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Food distribution", "Daily delivery", "Split case ordering", "24/7 customer support", "Online ordering platform", "Mobile ordering app", "Fresh-cut produce processing", "PrepKitchen operations", "Local food sourcing", "Direct seafood sourcing"], "industries": ["Foodservice", "Restaurants", "Schools", "Healthcare", "Hospitality", "Retail"], "materials": ["Fresh produce", "Seafood", "Meat", "Dairy", "Gourmet products", "Pantry staples", "To-go and paper essentials", "Fresh-cut fruits and vegetables"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Daily delivery (6-day service)", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["No minimum order size", "Split-case ordering", "Six-day weekly delivery in most markets", "24/7 customer support (call, text, chat, email)", "Proprietary online ordering platform and mobile app", "PrepKitchen fresh-cut produce processing"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Lexington, Kentucky -> db", "Founder and CEO Ron Turnier -> /quality", "19 distribution centers across 12 states -> /", "Serves over 16,000 restaurants -> /", "Seven product lines: produce, seafood, meat, gourmet, staples, to-go, dairy -> /", "No minimum order size -> /", "Split cases option -> /", "6-day delivery service -> /", "24/7 customer support via call, text, chat, email -> /", "Online ordering platform and mobile app -> /", "Acquisition of Quality Cut Produce (Sept 9, 2026) -> /quality", "PrepKitchen fresh-cut produce operation expanded -> /quality", "Serves restaurants, schools, healthcare, hosp